abstract: >-
  AMM (Python package amm) is a Python library, command line, browser application and MCP interface for designing cubic periodic cells
  (triply periodic minimal surfaces, strut lattices and resonators) against stiffness, solid-fraction and complete
  elastic-wave band-gap targets in physical units. Search-tier estimates are kept apart from a checker that issues
  certificates from periodic homogenization across resolutions and grid offsets and from Bloch-mode counts at the
  claimed gap edges, refutes candidates, proves requests infeasible under named bounds, or records why it cannot
  decide. The runtime data set amm-data/1 (search atlas and error model) is attached to the release under CC-BY-4.0.
